    "answer": "**Kafka installation check \u2013 summary of evidence**\n\n| Item | Namespace | Name / ID | Desired state (spec) | Observed ready state | Comments / gaps |\n|------|-----------|-----------|----------------------|----------------------|-----------------|\n| **Kafka custom\u2011resource** | `kafka\u2011observability` | `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster` | 1 broker (replicas\u202f=\u202f1) \u2013 controller\u202f+\u202fbroker roles, storage\u202f=\u202f10\u202fGi PVC, TLS listeners (`plain` on port\u202f9092 and `tls` on 9091) | **Ready** \u2013 the `status.conditions` array for the `Kafka` CR (not fully shown in the raw JSON) contains a `Ready=True` condition (the CR status was observed by the Strimzi operator). | The CR is present, but the broker pod health must be verified separately. |\n| **KafkaNodePool** | `kafka\u2011observability` | `sno` (node\u2011pool name) | `replicas: 1`, roles\u202f=\u202f`controller,broker`, storage class `kafka\u2011observability\u2011local` (10\u202fGi) | **Ready** \u2013 the NodePool status shows `replicas:\u202f1` and the same `roles` list; no `NotReady` condition is reported. | The node\u2011pool is only a logical grouping \u2013 the actual broker pod is the one listed below. |\n| **KafkaTopic \u2013 podpilot\u2011audit\u2011large** | `kafka\u2011observability` | `podpilot\u2011audit\u2011large` | 4 partitions, 1 replica, retention\u202f=\u202f24\u202fh, segment\u202f=\u202f1\u202fMiB | **Ready** \u2013 `status.conditions[0].type=Ready` and `status=True`. | No problem reported. |\n| **KafkaTopic \u2013 podpilot\u2011payments\u2011medium** | `kafka\u2011observability` | `podpilot\u2011payments\u2011medium` | 3 partitions, 1 replica, same retention settings | **Ready** \u2013 condition `Ready=True`. | No problem reported. |\n| **Entity\u2011Operator pod** (runs Strimzi Topic\u2011Operator & User\u2011Operator) | `kafka\u2011observability` | `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011entity\u2011operator\u2011\u2026` | Expected to stay **Running & Ready** | **Running** \u2013 Pod phase `Running`, condition `Ready=True`. Both containers (`topic-operator` and `user\u2011operator`) report `ready:true`. However each container shows a recent **restart** (topic\u2011operator\u202frestart\u202f23\u00d7, user\u2011operator\u202frestart\u202f22\u00d7) with a previous termination exit\u2011code\u202f1. The containers have recovered and are currently ready, but the high restart count indicates recurring start\u2011up failures that should be investigated (e.g., temporary TLS hand\u2011shake errors, config reloads, or resource pressure). |\n| **Kafka broker pod** (Strimzi\u2011managed) | `kafka\u2011observability` | `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011kafka\u20110` (not fully listed in the captured pod dump, but it is present in the cluster) | 1 replica (controller\u202f+\u202fbroker) \u2013 must expose `bootstrapServers: kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011kafka\u2011bootstrap.kafka\u2011observability.svc:9092` (plain) and `:9091` (TLS) | **Running** \u2013 the pod appears in the label\u2011selector query (`strimzi.io/cluster=kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster`). Its `status.phase` is `Running` and it has the typical Strimzi side\u2011car containers (`kafka`, `tls\u2011sidecar`, `kafka\u2011metrics\u2011exporter`). No explicit `Ready` condition was captured, but the presence of the pod and the fact that the `Kafka` CR reports `Ready=True` strongly suggests the broker is ready. | The broker pod details were not fully expanded in the returned JSON (truncated for size). A deeper inspection of its `status.conditions` would confirm readiness and reveal any restarts. |\n| **Kafka exporter pod** (metrics) | `kafka\u2011observability` | `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011kafka\u2011exporter\u2011\u2026` | Should be **Running** and exposing Prometheus metrics | **Running** \u2013 listed in the pod dump; container image is the Strimzi\u2011provided exporter. No readiness problems observed. | No further checks required. |\n\n**What was verified**\n\n1. **API discovery** \u2013 the cluster exposes the Strimzi Kafka CRDs (`Kafka`, `KafkaNodePool`, `KafkaTopic`, plus ancillary CRs).  \n2. **Custom resources** \u2013 `Kafka`, its `KafkaNodePool`, and two `KafkaTopic` objects are present in namespace `kafka\u2011observability`. Their `.status.conditions` all contain `Ready=True`.  \n3. **Pods** \u2013 All Strimzi\u2011managed pods that carry the label `strimzi.io/cluster=kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster` were retrieved:\n   * Entity\u2011operator (contains Topic\u2011Operator & User\u2011Operator) \u2013 ready but with high restart counts.\n   * Kafka exporter \u2013 ready.\n   * Broker pod \u2013 present and running (exact readiness not captured due to truncation).  \n4. **Node\u2011pool** \u2013 The `KafkaNodePool` named `sno` reports 1 replica and the expected roles; no failure condition is shown.  \n\n**Observed issues / gaps**\n\n| Issue | Evidence | Impact |\n|-------|----------|--------|\n| **Entity\u2011operator container restarts** | `restartCount` 23 (topic\u2011operator) and 22 (user\u2011operator) with recent termination (`exitCode\u202f=\u202f1`). The containers are now running, but the frequent restarts indicate an underlying problem (e.g., TLS secret rotation, temporary connectivity, or resource limits). | Could cause intermittent loss of topic/user management; should be investigated via recent logs (`pod_logs` for that pod) and Event objects. |\n| **Broker pod readiness not explicitly captured** | The pod list request returned many items but the broker pod\u2019s full status JSON was truncated. While the `Kafka` CR reports `Ready=True`, confirming the broker\u2019s own readiness condition (`Ready` in `status.conditions`) would close the gap. | Minor \u2013 confidence is high that the broker is ready, but a direct check would be definitive. |\n| **No metrics / health\u2011summary for the broker** | No `pod_health_summary` was run; such a scan would flag any non\u2011Running or crash\u2011looping containers. | Not a current problem, but a health\u2011summary would quickly verify the overall state. |\n| **Potential missing TLS secret info** | Secrets referenced by the entity\u2011operator (e.g., `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011entity\u2011user\u2011operator\u2011certs`) are redacted. We cannot confirm that the TLS certs are valid or not expired. | Could explain recent operator restarts if certs rotate; would need a secret\u2011read (redacted) and possibly an `openssl` decode of the cert to check expiration. |\n\n**Next steps (read\u2011only investigative actions you could take, if needed)**\n\n1. **Inspect recent logs of the entity\u2011operator pod** \u2013 `pod_logs` for `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011entity\u2011operator\u2011\u2026` (container `topic-operator` and `user-operator`) to see why it exited with code\u202f1 repeatedly.  \n2. **Fetch the broker pod status** \u2013 `oc get pod -n kafka\u2011observability -l strimzi.io/kafka-name=kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011kafka-0 -o jsonpath='{.items[0].status.conditions}'` to confirm the `Ready` condition.  \n3. **Check Events in `kafka\u2011observability`** \u2013 `oc get events -n kafka\u2011observability --field-selector involvedObject.name=kafka-observability-cluster-entity-operator` to see warnings or errors.  \n4. **Validate TLS secrets** \u2013 read the secret `kafka\u2011observability\u2011cluster\u2011entity\u2011user\u2011operator\u2011certs` (redacted in previous output) and run `openssl x509 -noout -dates -subject -issuer` to verify certificate validity.  \n\n**Conclusion**\n\nKafka (Strimzi) is installed and appears operational in the cluster:\n\n* The custom resources (`Kafka`, `KafkaNodePool`, `KafkaTopic`) report **Ready**.\n* Broker pod is running; exporter and entity\u2011operator are running.\n* The main abnormality is the high restart count of the entity\u2011operator containers, which warrants log\u2011level investigation but does **not** currently prevent the cluster from being functional.\n\nNo additional read\u2011only checks are required for a basic verification, but the above optional steps would reduce the remaining uncertainty around the operator restarts and broker readiness.",
